{"mem_mpzacxn5_cc42afedfd55":{"concepts":[],"content":"This is a test memory for Antigravity integration.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T09:21:24.300Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzacxn5_cc42afedfd55","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"This is a test memory for Antigravity integration.","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T09:21:24.300Z","version":1},"mem_mpzc07mk_3cf9010e59d5":{"concepts":["FocusLock","OTP","Brevo","ADB reverse","architecture"],"content":"FocusLock uses a local Node.js backend (port 3000) for sending OTPs via Brevo Email API. The Android app connects to it via adb reverse tcp:3000 tcp:3000 using http://127.0.0.1:3000. It uses cleartext traffic enabled in network security config. The app blocking mechanisms are Accessibility Service, Local VPN (on-device, no external server), and Device Admin. Data is stored in Room. Twilio was replaced with Brevo Email OTP to avoid costs. The project is managed heavily by markdown artifacts and agent rules.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T10:07:29.908Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzc07mk_3cf9010e59d5","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"FocusLock uses a local Node.js backend (port 3000) for sending OTPs via Brevo Em","type":"architecture","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T10:07:29.908Z","version":1},"mem_mpzc70d0_b60d3d41bdd4":{"concepts":["Network Security","Android manifest","Cleartext traffic","ADB port forwarding"],"content":"The FocusLock Android app uses a custom Network Security Configuration (network_security_config.xml) and modifies AndroidManifest.xml to allow cleartext HTTP traffic during debug builds. This was necessary to allow the physical Android device to connect to the local Node.js backend running on 127.0.0.1 (via adb reverse tcp:3000 tcp:3000) instead of using the emulator IP 10.0.2.2. Production builds will use HTTPS.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T10:12:47.120Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzc70d0_b60d3d41bdd4","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"The FocusLock Android app uses a custom Network Security Configuration (network_","type":"architecture","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T10:12:47.120Z","version":1},"mem_mpzc712e_f7739ab092fc":{"concepts":["UI Flow","Onboarding","OTP Verification","Navigation Graph"],"content":"The FocusLock onboarding and setup flow was recently refactored. The OTP / Trusted Contact Verification step was moved to occur AFTER Timer Setup and Keyword Selection, rather than immediately after Permissions. E.164 phone number fields were refactored to use email addresses throughout DTOs, Room entities, and UI state to support the migration to Brevo Email API. The HasVerifiedContactUseCase allows returning users to skip redundant OTP checks.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T10:12:48.036Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzc712e_f7739ab092fc","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"The FocusLock onboarding and setup flow was recently refactored. The OTP / Trust","type":"architecture","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T10:12:48.036Z","version":1},"mem_mpzci6eb_fc926961bc79":{"concepts":["Development Environment","CLI","No Android Studio","VS Code","ADB"],"content":"FocusLock is being developed in a restricted environment without Admin rights and without Android Studio. The workflow relies entirely on Command-Line Tools (Gradle wrapper, sdkmanager), VS Code, and physical Android device testing via USB debugging. This setup is preferred because Accessibility Service, VPN Service, and Device Admin features require a real device to function correctly.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T10:21:28.129Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzci6eb_fc926961bc79","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"FocusLock is being developed in a restricted environment without Admin rights an","type":"architecture","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T10:21:28.129Z","version":1},"mem_mpzci7ew_402de7e1424b":{"concepts":["Multi-Agent Roster","MASTER.md","Rules","Kiro"],"content":"The project strictly enforces a 12-agent roster defined in MASTER.md (located in .kiro/agents/). This includes the Architect Agent, Domain Agent (strictly no Android imports), Data Layer Agent, Room Database Agent, Accessibility Agent, VPN Agent, WorkManager Agent, Backend API Agent, Security Agent, Testing Agent, and Code Reviewer Agent. Tasks must be routed to the correct agent before writing code, and Security/Code Reviewer agents must validate sensitive changes.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T10:21:29.476Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzci7ew_402de7e1424b","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"The project strictly enforces a 12-agent roster defined in MASTER.md (located in","type":"workflow","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T10:21:29.476Z","version":1},"mem_mpzci7vj_6ed28c7344c7":{"concepts":["Codebase Graph","Leiden communities","Blast Radius","God Nodes"],"content":"FocusLock uses a highly modular Clean Architecture. The codebase graph analysis identified 15 major functional Leiden communities. Key 'God Nodes' with massive architectural blast radii include: BlockingRepositoryImpl, BlockingRepository, SessionDao, UnlockRequestDao, BlockedDomainDao, BlockedKeywordDao, and TrustedContactDao. The execution flows heavily rely on Jetpack Compose UI triggering Domain UseCases, which map to Data Repositories and Room SQL.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T10:21:30.074Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzci7vj_6ed28c7344c7","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"FocusLock uses a highly modular Clean Architecture. The codebase graph analysis ","type":"architecture","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T10:21:30.074Z","version":1},"mem_mpzcmfsl_f16631edee5f":{"concepts":["architecture","focuslocker","android","block","vpn","accessibility"],"content":"FocusLocker is an Android Focus & Blocker App built using Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Coroutines, Hilt, and Room (Flow). It enforces digital wellness by blocking distracting content during a user-set session. The core blocking mechanisms rely on an Android Accessibility Service (reads URL bars to block keywords) and an on-device VPN Service (intercepts DNS to block entire domains). The Android Device Admin API prevents uninstallation during an active session. Only one session can be ACTIVE at any time, governed by the expires_at timestamp.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T10:24:46.889Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzcmfsl_f16631edee5f","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"FocusLocker is an Android Focus & Blocker App built using Kotlin, Jetpack Compos","type":"architecture","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T10:24:46.889Z","version":1},"mem_mpzcmx3f_fd5e3cd422c4":{"concepts":["navigation","workflow","otp flow","ui"],"content":"The onboarding and session creation navigation flow is structured as: Onboarding -> Permissions -> CategorySelection -> KeywordSelection -> TimerSetup -> TrustedContactSetup -> VerifyContact(OTP) -> SessionConfirmation -> ActiveSession. This ensures that the user selects categories and timers before assigning a trusted contact and verifying via OTP. The HasVerifiedContactUseCase allows returning users to bypass setup steps.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T10:25:09.382Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzcmx3f_fd5e3cd422c4","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"The onboarding and session creation navigation flow is structured as: Onboarding","type":"workflow","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T10:25:09.382Z","version":1},"mem_mpzcmxoj_98d5b9a45b4a":{"concepts":["otp","email","brevo","backend","debugging","adb reverse"],"content":"The OTP system for FocusLocker was migrated from SMS (Twilio) to Email using the Brevo API. The backend requires BREVO_API_KEY and BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL. During local development on a physical device, 'adb reverse tcp:3000 tcp:3000' is required to forward traffic to the Node.js backend. The Android app accesses the backend via the local machine IP (e.g. 192.168.41.113) or forwarded port 3000. DTOs and database entities (TrustedContactEntity) have been refactored to use 'email' rather than 'phoneNumber'.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T10:25:10.141Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzcmxoj_98d5b9a45b4a","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"The OTP system for FocusLocker was migrated from SMS (Twilio) to Email using the","type":"architecture","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T10:25:10.141Z","version":1},"mem_mpzcn4km_4af75c29835e":{"concepts":["vpn","dns","testing","modernization","gradle","room"],"content":"FocusLocker build pipeline has been modernized to Kotlin 2.0.0, AGP 8.7.3, and uses the official Gradle Compose Compiler plugin. Room schema exports are configured via KSP. The VPN Service routes primary DNS traffic to 8.8.8.8 and fallback to 8.8.4.4, with non-DNS traffic passing through. Current limitations: missing unit tests for SessionTimerWorker, SessionExpiryWorker, BootReceiver, and SessionNotificationManager. Release build configurations (ProGuard, signing) remain unverified. A warning is needed for Private DNS (DNS-over-TLS) bypassing standard VPN interception.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T10:25:19.072Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzcn4km_4af75c29835e","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"FocusLocker build pipeline has been modernized to Kotlin 2.0.0, AGP 8.7.3, and u","type":"architecture","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T10:25:19.072Z","version":1},"mem_mpzer888_dcda4ff0bb09":{"concepts":["FocusLock","Session Lifecycle","Data Model","OTP Flow","VPN","Architecture"],"content":"FocusLock is an Android app that helps users voluntarily block distracting or harmful browser content for a self-set time period.\nKey components:\n1. Android Accessibility Service â€” reads browser URL bars to detect and block keyword matches across all browsers.\n2. Local on-device VPN (no external server) â€” intercepts DNS to block entire domains by category.\n3. Android Device Admin API â€” prevents the app from being uninstalled during an active session.\nBackend: Node.js/Express/TypeScript generating and verifying OTPs via Twilio Email/SMS with in-memory storage (no DB) and 10-minute TTL.\nApp stack: Kotlin 2.0.0, Jetpack Compose, Coroutines, Hilt, Room, Retrofit, WorkManager.\nDatabase constraints: Only one session can have `status = ACTIVE` at any time. `expires_at` is the single source of truth.\nSession Lifecycle: Activation -> ACTIVE -> Expiry Worker / Timer -> COMPLETED. If user tries to create a new session and there is a stale ACTIVE session (past expires_at), the system auto-completes it via DeactivateSessionUseCase before creating the new one.\nOTP Flow: OTP is requested for early unlock. Verification happens via Node.js backend. User enters email -> OTP sent -> User verifies OTP -> Session unlocked early.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T11:24:29.620Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzer888_dcda4ff0bb09","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"FocusLock is an Android app that helps users voluntarily block distracting or ha","type":"architecture","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T11:24:29.620Z","version":1},"mem_mpzgg3az_195a27912ae9":{"concepts":["android","kotlin","compose","hilt","room","workmanager","vpn","accessibility","device-admin","twilio","otp"],"content":"FocuseLocker is a production Android focus/blocker app. Tech stack: Kotlin-only, Jetpack Compose (no XML), Hilt DI, Room + Flow, Retrofit + OkHttp + Kotlin Serialization, WorkManager for timers, Node.js/Express/TypeScript backend with Twilio OTP. Three core mechanisms: (1) Accessibility Service for browser URL monitoring, (2) On-device VPN for DNS blocking, (3) Device Admin API to prevent uninstall during active session. Backend stores NOTHING permanently â€” OTPs live in-memory with 10-min TTL only.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T12:11:49.288Z","files":["app/src/main/java/com/focuslock","backend/src/server.ts"],"id":"mem_mpzgg3az_195a27912ae9","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"FocuseLocker is a production Android focus/blocker app. Tech stack: Kotlin-only,","type":"architecture","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T12:11:49.288Z","version":1},"mem_mpzgg73x_173f8bd23382":{"concepts":["session","hasActiveSession","expiresAt","bug","Room","DAO","lifecycle","expiry"],"content":"CRITICAL BUG FIXED (conv e7071875): SessionRepositoryImpl.hasActiveSession() was only checking status = ACTIVE but NOT checking expiresAt > now(). This caused \"Session Still Active\" error when trying to start a new session after a previous one expired. Fix: Added expiresAt timestamp check so expired sessions are NOT treated as active. SessionDao queries were also updated to account for expiration time.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T12:11:54.234Z","files":["app/src/main/java/com/focuslock/data/repository/SessionRepositoryImpl.kt","app/src/main/java/com/focuslock/domain/usecase/IsSessionActiveUseCase.kt"],"id":"mem_mpzgg73x_173f8bd23382","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"CRITICAL BUG FIXED (conv e7071875): SessionRepositoryImpl.hasActiveSession() was","type":"bug","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T12:11:54.234Z","version":1},"mem_mpzgg7hp_3d5ab124b734":{"concepts":["kotlin","rules","conventions","DAO","flow","ViewModel","OTP","session","keywords"],"content":"FocuseLocker non-negotiable coding rules: (1) No !! in Kotlin, (2) No logic in Composables, (3) No business logic in ViewModels â€” only state and UseCase delegation, (4) All DAO reads return Flow<T>, (5) No runBlocking in production, (6) Never log phone numbers or OTPs even in debug, (7) Backend URL must come from BuildConfig â€” never hardcoded, (8) Only one ACTIVE session at any time â€” enforced in code, (9) Keywords stored lowercase always, (10) Max 50 custom keywords for MVP.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T12:11:54.727Z","files":[".kiro/agents/master.md"],"id":"mem_mpzgg7hp_3d5ab124b734","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"FocuseLocker non-negotiable coding rules: (1) No !! in Kotlin, (2) No logic in C","type":"preference","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T12:11:54.727Z","version":1},"mem_mpzky1dn_56bb1507f778":{"concepts":["architecture","refactor","session-management","lifecycle","hilt","circular-dependency"],"content":"Resolved 'Session Still Active' bug and improved Session Lifecycle Architecture.\n1. Introduced `CleanupStaleSessionUseCase` to act as the single source of truth for checking if a session is stale (expiresAt < now) and calling `DeactivateSessionUseCase`. This eliminated a potential Hilt circular dependency where `ActivateSessionUseCase` depended directly on `DeactivateSessionUseCase`.\n2. Updated `ActivateSessionUseCase` and `IsSessionActiveUseCase` to delegate to `CleanupStaleSessionUseCase`.\n3. Updated `InitializeAppUseCase` to trigger `cleanupStaleSessionUseCase()` on app launch. This ensures the database is purged of any stale ACTIVE sessions before onboarding or routing logic proceeds.\n4. Enforced rule that `SessionDao.getActiveSessionSync()` gets any ACTIVE session regardless of expiry, leaving expiry validation and cleanup entirely to the UseCase layer.","createdAt":"2026-06-04T14:17:45.001Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mpzky1dn_56bb1507f778","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Resolved 'Session Still Active' bug and improved Session Lifecycle Architecture.","type":"architecture","updatedAt":"2026-06-04T14:17:45.001Z","version":1},"mem_mrj8otg4_091c823a727b":{"concepts":["unit tests","DnsConfigTest","PermissionSetupViewModelTest","bug fix","NPE","mockk"],"content":"Resolved two unit test failures in the FocuseLocker project. 1. In DnsConfigTest, fixed a ComparisonFailure by updating the mocked SharedPreferences return value from 'mock-id-123' to 'mockid123' to match the sanitization output. 2. In PermissionSetupViewModelTest, fixed NullPointerExceptions by mocking the newly introduced OemBatteryOptimizationHelper dependency and returning emptyList() for getBatteryOptimizationIntentsList(any()). All fixes verified via ./gradlew testDebugUnitTest.","createdAt":"2026-07-13T13:09:45.357Z","files":["app/src/test/java/com/focuslock/service/vpn/DnsConfigTest.kt","app/src/test/java/com/focuslock/ui/onboarding/PermissionSetupViewModelTest.kt"],"id":"mem_mrj8otg4_091c823a727b","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Resolved two unit test failures in the FocuseLocker project. 1. In DnsConfigTest","type":"bug","updatedAt":"2026-07-13T13:09:45.357Z","version":1},"mem_mrj8spba_2d5d94eeb4df":{"concepts":["chat_context_log.md","session log","detailed context","artifacts"],"content":"The detailed chat context and session log for fixing DnsConfigTest and PermissionSetupViewModelTest was successfully written to the artifact file: chat_context_log.md in the brain directory (fc6db141-57e5-467e-9b85-68de1662fd29).","createdAt":"2026-07-13T13:12:46.626Z","files":["C:\\Users\\harshal.bhoyar\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\fc6db141-57e5-467e-9b85-68de1662fd29\\chat_context_log.md"],"id":"mem_mrj8spba_2d5d94eeb4df","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"The detailed chat context and session log for fixing DnsConfigTest and Permissio","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-07-13T13:12:46.626Z","version":1},"mem_mrj92qzt_6cf32702f1de":{"concepts":["agentmemory rule","project name inclusion","semantic search optimization","memory export","global context rule"],"content":"GLOBAL RULE FOR AGENT MEMORY: Whenever saving a new memory or recalling an existing one, the content and concepts MUST explicitly include the name of the project (e.g., 'FocuseLocker' or 'Harshal-S-Bhoyar/FocuseLocker'). This ensures that even if the memory database is exported to another tool, or when a semantic search is performed, every memory remains perfectly scoped and identifiable by its associated project. Never save a memory without mentioning the project name in the actual content body.","createdAt":"2026-07-13T13:20:35.365Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mrj92qzt_6cf32702f1de","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"GLOBAL RULE FOR AGENT MEMORY: Whenever saving a new memory or recalling an exist","type":"pattern","updatedAt":"2026-07-13T13:20:35.365Z","version":1},"mem_mrj939i9_15d3a5203c67":{"concepts":[],"content":"Always use the project name 'Harshal-S-Bhoyar/FocuseLocker' when saving or recalling memory. This ensures all content is correctly scoped to the project, making semantic search work properly even if exported to other tools.","createdAt":"2026-07-13T13:20:59.357Z","files":[],"id":"mem_mrj939i9_15d3a5203c67","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"Always use the project name 'Harshal-S-Bhoyar/FocuseLocker' when saving or recal","type":"preference","updatedAt":"2026-07-13T13:20:59.357Z","version":1},"mem_mrjad7pc_86351c86da2b":{"concepts":["chat_context_log.md","session log","detailed context","dynamic mcp configuration","test setup"],"content":"The mcp_config.json dynamic configuration was verified for agentmemory. Testing setup initiated: Gradle daemon stopped, unit tests run, and androidTest boilerplate created. Context log saved.","createdAt":"2026-07-13T13:56:43.195Z","files":["C:\\Users\\harshal.bhoyar\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\fc6db141-57e5-467e-9b85-68de1662fd29\\chat_context_log.md"],"id":"mem_mrjad7pc_86351c86da2b","isLatest":true,"sessionIds":[],"sourceObservationIds":[],"strength":7,"supersedes":[],"title":"The mcp_config.json dynamic configuration was verified for agentmemory. Testing ","type":"fact","updatedAt":"2026-07-13T13:56:43.195Z","version":1}}ˆ9␀¸±ÿÿ